A Record in Stone
[vignette dungeons/brides_cave]

FIXME(mundane): PC pauses in a branching wet tunnel to take bearings and brings the lantern close to the carved wall. The tunnel bends, splits, rejoins — no surface logic to it.
FIXME(mundane): The wall is covered in inscriptions: love oaths, prayers, names, regrets, tally marks. The script shifts every few paces — fine calligraphy, jagged scrawls, deep gouges. Some passages end mid-word, the final letter trailing off. Newer words carved directly atop older ones, layer on layer.
FIXME(dread): A single name appears inscribed a hundred times over. Messages to family. Regrets for things unsaid and misdeeds. Tally marks in columns — five-bar gates by the hundreds, scored hard into the stone.
FIXME(dread): Two quoted oath-fragments are legible: one calling down spirits to judge a man named Alain; one addressed to Matthis, the writer keeping vigil with their last candle. Both end in the register of someone who has run out of recourse.
